                    <death when="1812-02-28"/>
                    <occupation>playwright</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>John Till Allingham was a playwright of Irish extraction who had a significant success with <title>Fortune's Frolic</title> (Covent Garden, 1799).</p>
                        <p>There are two entries, both associated with <persName key="ROB04">Mary Robinson</persName>.  
    Godwin clearly knew his work and he attended several of his plays. The use of an apostrophe in the first entry suggests that there 
    is more than one Allingham.  Allingham did not marry, but his sister was the actress Maria Caroline Allingham (d. 1811). It is possible that 
    this entry includes her.</p>
                    </note>
